@@ -18,3 +18,11 @@ the discount as `discountCents`, and its `totalCents` is the items minus the dis
 Apply a code with `orders.applyCode(orderNumber, code)`. An unknown code, or `WELCOME5` on a smaller order, is refused
 with the reason and the order is left as it was. The discount never touches shipping: whether an order ships free is
 decided on its items before any discount.
+
+## Monthly export
+
+The accountant loads the orders of each month into her spreadsheet. `orders.exportMonth('YYYY-MM')` gives that month's
+orders as CSV text: a header line, then one line per order placed in the month, by order number. The columns are
+`order`, `date`, `customer` and `total`, where `total` is what the customer pays in euros with two decimals (the items,
+minus any discount, plus the shipping). Customers' email addresses and phone numbers are not exported. A value holding a comma, a quote or a line break is quoted,
+and a month with no orders gives the header alone. A month not written `YYYY-MM` is refused with the reason.
